{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "The current best (config_031: scvi_n200, multimodal, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted, acc=0.678) outperforms the best RNA-only baseline (config_002: pca_n2000, rna_only, multiprofile, avgpool, acc=0.591) by 0.087, but this gap conflates three factors: RNA encoder upgrade (pca→scvi), image modality addition, and weighted fusion. We lack a direct RNA-only scvi_n200 multiprofile avgpool baseline. Config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean single-variable change from config_002, isolating the RNA encoder effect. Critically, comparing config_005 to config_031 will quantify how much the image modality (resnet50 + weighted fusion) actually contributes on top of the best RNA representation. If config_005 approaches ~0.63, the image adds only ~0.05 and further image-encoder investment (e.g., ViT-L) is low-priority; if it stays near 0.59, the image contributes substantially and upgrading the image encoder (config_037) becomes the clear next step. Under a limited budget, this single experiment resolves the most important open question—whether the image modality is worth further investment—while also providing the RNA encoder comparison we lack."
}

